  "headline_checks": {
    "F1": "Actual independent array is transported to the product of its marginal laws, then tilted by the exact product Esscher density. Independent-copy squared-difference identities yield exp(+-4delta|t|) variance bounds. Actual fourth cumulants, bounded-derivative Taylor estimates, saddlepoint inversion and the tv cubic cancellation yield the displayed cubic log correction. Berry--Esseen is applied under the actual standardized tilted law. The strict Laplace identity excludes atoms at zero and handles s=0 separately, including all x>=0 without an un-tilted small-x shortcut. Both positive constants are fixed before every law/model/threshold.",
    "F2": "The two independent pairs may live on distinct spaces. The actual leading CDF approximation is precisely the printed hypothesis, rather than an assumed conclusion about shifted laws. Product-law conditioning proves the actual shifted CDF identity. Global C2 Taylor works for signed shifts, finite second moments give all needed integrability, and subtraction has the correct Fprime(t)(EV-EU) sign. No shift centering, nonnegativity or four-way independence is added.",
    "F3": "The primitive probabilities and amplitude construct an actual finite product law with independent Rademacher signs, one observation activation and per-coordinate masks. The output property structure contains actual i.i.d./central symmetry/centering/unit moments, explicit covariance, exact rank and gap, literal fourth moments, all q>=1 envelope moments, and the actual Gaussian factor/law with both width bounds. The added raw and Gaussian covariance theorems identify the intended unnormalized observation and Gaussian laws directly. r=1 remains allowed; m>=2 is enough to attain the largest off-diagonal correlation."
  },
  "method_qualifications": [
    {
      "passage": "F1.saddlepoint",
      "finding": "The actual terminal route obtains a root in [0,2x] by local Taylor+IVT. Separate checked strict-monotonicity/uniqueness and printed-interval theorems recover the displayed interval conclusion. This is an equivalent constructive root selection, not a premise supplying the root."
    },
    {
      "passage": "F1.relative-log-error",
      "finding": "The actual terminal route bounds log J(s)-log J(x) by |s-x|/min(s,x), using s comparable to x>0. Together with the checked cancellation it has the required O(delta^2*x^2) error. The sharper printed log-derivative and derivative-decay displays are separately proved in LowerLemmaF1Support, rather than claimed as terminal dependencies."
    }
  ],
